## Setting up Better Auth

1. Generate and set the `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` environment variable in your `.env.local`:

   ```bash
   <%- getPackageManagerExecuteScript('@better-auth/cli', ['secret']) %>
   ```

2. Visit the [Better Auth documentation](https://www.better-auth.com) to unlock the full potential of authentication in your app.

<% if (addOnEnabled.drizzle || addOnEnabled.prisma) { %>
### Create the auth tables

Better Auth uses your <%= addOnEnabled.drizzle ? 'Drizzle' : 'Prisma' %> database. Its user, session, account, and verification tables are included in <%= addOnEnabled.drizzle ? '`src/db/schema.ts`' : '`prisma/schema.prisma`' %>.

Set `DATABASE_URL` in `.env.local`, then <% if (addOnEnabled.prisma) { %>run the `db:generate` package script to update the Prisma client and <% } %>run the `db:push` package script to create the tables. Use the ORM's migration workflow when deploying schema changes to an existing database.
<% } else { %>
### Adding a Database (Optional)

Better Auth can work in stateless mode, but to persist user data, add a database:

```typescript
// src/lib/auth.ts
import { betterAuth } from "better-auth";
import { Pool } from "pg";

export const auth = betterAuth({
  database: new Pool({
    connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL,
  }),
  // ... rest of config
});
```

Then run migrations:

```bash
<%- getPackageManagerExecuteScript('@better-auth/cli', ['migrate']) %>
```

<% } %>
